      "reason": "Approve the current merged assignment. p002: 興 in jinshu 119 s0003 「姚泓，字元子，興之長子也。」 is Yao Hong's father Yao Xing, and 興 in s0027 「興既死，秘不發喪。」 records his death before Hong's accession (s0031 以義熙十二年僭即帝位). p117: its only basis is the same validated p002 興 span in s0003 (personal name 姚興; descriptive 'Father of Yao Hong'). It has no mention of its own and is the same individual, as my accepted one-pair merge decision found. Hong has only one father in the chapter, so no second person is involved. Anchor jinshu:117:p001: the Yao Xing biography heading 「姚興」 (117 s0001) and 「姚興，字子略，萇之長子也。」 (117 s0003) name Yao Chang's eldest son Yao Xing, the ruler whose son and successor is Yao Hong in jinshu 119. This matches both targets: same name, same dynasty and same father-son line, with no contradiction. No false merge or wrong actor among the targets. unresolvedIdentity stays true: retrieval overflowed (zh:姚㒷, 60 dossiers, 8 visited), and other cross-chapter Yao Xing records, including jinshu 119 p193 子略 and p201 興, were not settled by this review. The other external protected members were not re-audited. No English repair is needed: s0003 and s0027 render 興 as Yao Xing.",
